+### Prized {#prized}
+
+Cloud Linux VMs ("boxes") that you run OpenClaw on yourself, created and managed with the `prized` CLI. A box can pause and resume.
+
+- **Guide**: [prized.dev/docs/openclaw](https://prized.dev/docs/openclaw)
+- **Price** (as of 2026-11-07): billed by the hour from a monthly plan of $10 to $1,000 that lands as credit. The size the guide uses, Micro (2 vCPU, 4 GB RAM, 80 GB disk), is $0.034/hour awake, about $25/month around the clock; asleep it pays only for its disk ($0.008/hour). New accounts get $30 of credit once, with no card ([billing](https://prized.dev/docs/billing))
+- **Locations**: Oregon, N. California, N. Virginia, Ohio, Frankfurt
+- **Features**: Ubuntu 24.04 with root and Docker; `systemctl --user` services start at boot and keep running after you log out; the Gateway stays on loopback and you reach the Control UI through an SSH tunnel
+- **Catch**: on the free credit a box auto-pauses after 2 hours idle, and a Gateway waiting for messages looks idle, so the guide turns auto-pause off for that box. While a box is paused, the assistant can't answer
+- **Local LLMs**: Possible on larger sizes (up to 32 vCPU, 128 GB RAM)
+
